An owner heartbeat's groups (#1110; core §7.5, observer 0.34 §7.3, §7.5).

The capture holds five puts on `lab/trio`'s owner heartbeat keys, written
by the model's writer (the fleet's `tests/owner_heartbeat.rs` regenerates
it): three groups on the `host` key, a known group beside an index the
catalog does not hold, one group on the `link` key, a put whose CH tag
is not 0, and a put written while its owner's clock guard holds, whose
time is the ahead time (core 0.113 §7.5). The key says which layout a put
carries, never its bytes.

Given the catalog its header names, each group is read with the revision its
index names (observer §7.5): its index, its tag and its size, then what it
vouches for. A group at an index the catalog does not hold is shown by its
envelope, and the put's other groups are read all the same. A put core §7.5
refuses whole is undecodable. The ahead time is shown as `time ahead`,
never as unknown and never as an instant (`freshness.v2` §5), and its
group is read as under any other time.

```console
$ zenctl echo --from tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.zrec --contracts ../zenkey/tests/contracts/trio --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.catalog.json --format table --color never
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
  zk2c owner heartbeat (host): host, run 0007, seq 3, time unknown, 3 groups | #0 alpha.v1, tag 11, 34 bits: state/status 0000000a vouched | #1 bravo.v1, tag 11, 34 bits: state/status 0000000b vouched | #2 charlie.v1, tag 1, 35 bits: state/status 0000000c vouched
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
  zk2c owner heartbeat (host): host, run 0007, seq 5, time unknown, 2 groups | #0 alpha.v1, tag 11, 34 bits: state/status 0000000a vouched | #900, tag 11, 34 bits: unread, unknown_index: the catalog holds no entry at its index (core §8.6)
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/link
  zk2c owner heartbeat (link): link, run 0007, seq 0, time unknown, 1 group | #2 charlie.v1, tag 1, 35 bits: state/reach 0000001c vouched
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
  <13 B that do not decode as zk2c owner heartbeat (host): the owner heartbeat is refused: tag>
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
  zk2c owner heartbeat (host): host, run 0007, seq 7, time ahead, 1 group | #0 alpha.v1, tag 11, 34 bits: state/status 0000000a vouched

```

The header keeps the catalog's id, epoch and lineage, and no entry. Without
`--catalog` no index can be read, so every group is shown by its envelope,
with the rung where its reading stopped.

```console
$ zenctl echo --from tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.zrec --contracts ../zenkey/tests/contracts/trio --format table --color never
reading tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.zrec under its header's catalog 53b44c4d (epoch 0), the recorder's word: give --catalog to read it through one of your own
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
  zk2c owner heartbeat (host): host, run 0007, seq 3, time unknown, 3 groups | #0, tag 11, 34 bits: unread, unknown_catalog: no catalog to read its index through (core §8.6): give the one its owner names | #1, tag 11, 34 bits: unread, unknown_catalog: no catalog to read its index through (core §8.6): give the one its owner names | #2, tag 1, 35 bits: unread, unknown_catalog: no catalog to read its index through (core §8.6): give the one its owner names
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
  zk2c owner heartbeat (host): host, run 0007, seq 5, time unknown, 2 groups | #0, tag 11, 34 bits: unread, unknown_catalog: no catalog to read its index through (core §8.6): give the one its owner names | #900, tag 11, 34 bits: unread, unknown_catalog: no catalog to read its index through (core §8.6): give the one its owner names
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/link
  zk2c owner heartbeat (link): link, run 0007, seq 0, time unknown, 1 group | #2, tag 1, 35 bits: unread, unknown_catalog: no catalog to read its index through (core §8.6): give the one its owner names
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
  <13 B that do not decode as zk2c owner heartbeat (host): the owner heartbeat is refused: tag>
zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
  zk2c owner heartbeat (host): host, run 0007, seq 7, time ahead, 1 group | #0, tag 11, 34 bits: unread, unknown_catalog: no catalog to read its index through (core §8.6): give the one its owner names

```

The ndjson form carries each group whole, and the ahead time as
`"time":"ahead"` where the unknown time is `null`.

```console
$ zenctl echo --from tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.zrec --contracts ../zenkey/tests/contracts/trio --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.catalog.json --format ndjson
