`timeline` keeps a class key's puts in one lane, by their key's run and seq.

```console
$ zenctl timeline --from tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.zrec --contracts ../zenkey/tests/contracts/trio --format table --color never
lab/trio freshness.v2 stream/heartbeats/{class} · arrival · no stamper; 5 stamped in band
0  +1.000s  in band run 0007, seq 3  zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
1  +2.000s  in band run 0007, seq 5  zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
2  +3.000s  in band run 0007, seq 0  zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/link
3  +4.000s  in band run 0007, seq 6  zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
4  +5.000s  in band run 0007, seq 7  zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host
ordered by arrival — observer monotonic, µs since window start; a position says when this observer saw a sample, never when it was produced (observer §8.3)
the per-publisher sequence-number lane is unavailable: zenoh 1.9/1.10 deliver no SourceInfo to subscribers (eclipse-zenoh/zenoh#2563); `tests/stamper.rs` pins it (observer §1)
@stream, @state, @op, @zk, @adv excluded from this window, not empty: no selector names them, and `*`/`**` never match a verbatim chunk (tooling guide O5)
no presence read stood behind these lanes: no owner's zid is named, so every stamp is unattributable (not foreign), and a key resolves past its address only through --contracts (tooling guide O7)
deliberately no edges: a merged ordering shows when things were seen on which clock, never that one caused another

```

A `--catalog` that does not read is refused with `--from` too, though a
capture's lanes are placed with none: the flag is never passed over.

```console
$ zenctl timeline --from tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.zrec --contracts ../zenkey/tests/contracts/trio --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/no-such-catalog.json --format table --color never
? 2
Error: --catalog tests/cmd/fixtures/no-such-catalog.json: No such file or directory (os error 2)

```

`replay` writes them back as it recorded them, in a namespace of its own.

```console
$ zenctl replay --dry-run --format table --color never --namespace replay tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.zrec
tests/cmd/fixtures/owner-heartbeat.zrec: captured zk2/lab/trio/** under base "" (2026-11-21T00:00:00Z)
would put replay/zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host  (33 B, zenoh/bytes)
would put replay/zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host  (26 B, zenoh/bytes)
would put replay/zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/link  (19 B, zenoh/bytes)
would put replay/zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host  (19 B, zenoh/bytes)
would put replay/zk2/lab/trio/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeats/host  (19 B, zenoh/bytes)
would replay 5 put(s) and 0 tombstone(s) from zk2/lab/trio/** (captured 2026-11-21T00:00:00Z)
into namespace "replay", each key moved from the capture's base ""

```
